  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given a binary string SSS, define f(S)=max⁡(#&nbsp;0s&nbsp;in&nbsp;S,&nbsp;#&nbsp;1s&nbsp;in&nbsp;S)f(S) = \\max ( \\text{\\# 0s in S, \\# 1s in S})f(S)=max(#&nbsp;0s&nbsp;in&nbsp;S,&nbsp;#&nbsp;1s&nbsp;in&nbsp;S), i.e. the the maximum among frequency of 000 and frequency of 111.\n\nFind the sum of fff over all substrings of SSS. Formally, compute ∑L=1N∑R=LNf(SLSL+1...SR)\\sum_{L = 1}^{N} \\sum_{R = L}^{N} f(S_L S_{L + 1} ... S_R)∑L=1N​∑R=LN​f(SL​SL+1​...SR​).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the size of the string\nThe second line of each test case contains SSS - the binary string.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the sum of fff over all substrings of SSS.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "∣S∣=N|S| = N∣S∣=N",
      "Si∈{0,1}S_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}Si​∈{0,1}",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n1\n0\n2\n01\n3\n110\n4\n0011\n6\n101101",
        "output": "1\n3\n8\n15\n38",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 2 : There are 333 substrings:\n\n000 : f(0)=1f(0) = 1f(0)=1\n111 : f(1)=1f(1) = 1f(1)=1\n010101 : f(01)=1f(01) = 1f(01)=1\n\nThus, the sum is 333."
      }
    ]
  },
